      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The scientific consensus is overwhelmingly in favor of dense, mixed-use, transit-oriented development (TOD) as the superior model for urban health and sustainability. Low-density, sprawling suburbs are inherently inefficient, driving up infrastructure costs and increasing carbon emissions. Therefore, cities must aggressively reform zoning codes to permit and encourage high-density housing near robust public transit networks. This approach is the most evidence-based path to solving both the housing crisis and environmental degradation simultaneously.",
      "source": "target",
